From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valix <djvalic.wc@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 26/26] ad5x: No stock-kernel rung; the recovery OS on p1's
 kernel; what was started in CPSPR

The boot rules no longer start the printer's stock 5.10 for the main
OS: 7.3 (opt-in) -> 6.6 -> the recovery OS. Two unconfirmed 6.6 starts
(one after an install) record 6.6 as failed; with no kernel of Kiln's
left (or two unconfirmed starts of a kernel this build doesn't know,
such as an older build's "stock") U-Boot points the flag at slot A and
starts the recovery OS. A state sector an older build wrote with
"kernel stock" reads as a kernel not known.

Slot A is checked as before (p1 a Linux uImage for MIPS with good CRCs
that isn't a U-Boot, p2 starting with "hsqs"). Kiln's main OS writes its
own 6.6 into p1 once this U-Boot has started it, so the recovery OS runs
on Kiln's 6.6; until then p1 holds the stock 5.10, which starts it as
well. A p1 kernel named "Linux-6.6-ad5x" gets "ad5x.kernel=own panic=10
loglevel=5" (no cmdline-extra); the watchdog stays stopped into the
recovery OS (its e2fsck can outlast the kernel's feeding).

When the rules would fall back but slot A isn't startable, the main OS
starts again with its own kernel whatever the records say (6.6, else
7.3), instead of the stock kernel; with no kernel at all U-Boot gives
up as before.

Before the jump U-Boot leaves 0x5500 | start count << 4 | what in CPSPR
instead of 0 (ad5x_start_uboot_kernel: 1 = 6.6, 2 = 7.3, 3 = recovery
OS, 0 = a bootm typed at the prompt). The SPL reads it as a fresh start,
as it read 0; Linux shows how the boot came up.
---
 arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h |  30 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c                    |  73 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.env                  |   4 ++--
 board/flashforge/ad5x/bootlogic.c               | 104 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 board/flashforge/ad5x/bootlogic.h               |  24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 5 files changed, 168 insertions(+), 67 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h
--- a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/include/mach/ad5x_start.h
@@ -39,7 +39,9 @@
  * SPL from a kernel slot); started otherwise (the stock SPL, a chainload
  * test) it writes SLOT_UBOOT for slot B, where Kiln puts it. Giving up
  * without a key (no eMMC, nothing to start): UBOOT_UP -> GAVE_UP, and
- * SLOT_UBOOT stays. Before it jumps to a kernel it writes 0.
+ * SLOT_UBOOT stays. Before it jumps to a kernel it writes a value of its
+ * own that says what it started (ad5x_start_uboot_kernel below), which
+ * the SPL reads as a fresh start.
  */
 #ifndef __MACH_AD5X_START_H__
 #define __MACH_AD5X_START_H__
@@ -167,4 +169,30 @@
 	return v;			/* SLOT_UBOOT: the other slot next */
 }
 
+/*
+ * What U-Boot proper leaves in CPSPR as it jumps to a kernel: 0x5500 | a
+ * low byte. Not 0x4b00-0x4bff, so the SPL's next start is a fresh one (as
+ * after 0); Linux writes its own value only when it reboots, so in Linux
+ * "devmem 0x10000034 32" shows how this boot was started:
+ *   bits 0-3  what (enum ad5x_ub_start)
+ *   bits 4-7  the main OS's start count in U-Boot's state (1-15, 15 for
+ *             15 or more), 0 for the others
+ * Neither Linux's reboot values (0x1a1a, 0x3535, 0x4343) nor Ingenic's
+ * SPLs' (0x4f5441, 0x41544f).
+ */
+#define AD5X_UB_MAGIC		0x5500u
+
+enum ad5x_ub_start {
+	AD5X_UB_BOOTM,		/* a bootm typed at the prompt */
+	AD5X_UB_MAIN_66,	/* the main OS on Kiln's 6.6 */
+	AD5X_UB_MAIN_73,	/* the main OS on mainline 7.3 */
+	AD5X_UB_RECOVERY,	/* the recovery OS (slot A) */
+};
+
+static inline unsigned int ad5x_start_uboot_kernel(unsigned int what,
+						   unsigned int tries)
+{
+	return AD5X_UB_MAGIC | (tries > 15 ? 15 : tries) << 4 | (what & 15);
+}
+
 #endif
